(
    title: "Extra Terrestrials",
    developer: Some("The Banting brothers"),
    description: Some("The rarest licensed-era cart on the system: a family-made Canadian game sold door-to-door around Southern Ontario in 1984 — roughly a hundred copies — then lost entirely until one surfaced at Brantford\'s Personal Computer Museum in 2011. The game itself is two-player only: one player steers an alien through the maze hoovering up dots while the other hunts it down, with a sprite that pointedly resembles a certain other extra-terrestrial."),
